general_notes.general_notes:
This study represents one of the largest neuroimaging investigations of hemispherotomy patients to date, with longitudinal pre- and post-surgery data. The normative modeling approach using 2115 healthy children from 11 datasets (ABIDE-I, ABIDE-II, BCP, CPMD, CBD, CCNP, HBN, HCPD, IBIS, PeriCBD, PING, Pixar) is crucial for controlling developmental confounds in pediatric populations. Complete dataset details: ABIDE-I (168 HC after QC, age 7-64, 17 sites, 3T), ABIDE-II (332 HC, age 5-64, 19 sites, 3T), BCP (257 HC, age 0-7, 6 sites, 3T), CPMD (90 HC, age 2-8, 1 site, 3T), CBD (69 HC, age 6-14, 2 sites, 3T), CCNP (116 HC, age 6-18, 1 site, 3T), HBN (76 HC, age 5-21, 3 sites, 1.5T/3T), HCPD (252 HC, age 5-21, 4 sites, 3T), IBIS (183 HC, age 0-3, 4 sites, 3T), PeriCBD (43 HC, age 3-10, 2 sites, 1.5T/3T), PING (415 HC, age 3-20, 10 sites, 3T), Pixar (114 HC, age 3-12, 1 site, 3T). Inclusion criteria for healthy subjects: aged 0.3-13 years, maximum 100 subjects per half-year interval, only highest quality image per subject for longitudinal data. Patients underwent peri-insular hemispherotomy (a functional hemispherotomy variant minimizing cortical resection). Etiology: left group 16 developmental/10 acquired/3 progressive, right group 22 developmental/5 acquired/1 progressive (p=0.17). Seizure outcomes excellent: 90% of left and 100% of right patients achieved Engel I at 3-month follow-up. Behavioral assessment used Griffiths Scales of Child Development III (5 domains: foundations of learning, language and communication, eye-hand coordination, personal-social-emotional, gross motor; mean correlation r=0.9; factorial analysis yielded one main factor accounting for 92.4% variance). MRI acquisition: Philips Achieva 3T, MPRAGE sequence, TR=8ms, TE=3.7ms, flip angle=8°, 220×220 matrix, 1mm slice thickness, 0.86×0.86×1.0mm voxels. Processing: longitudinal VBM with SPM12, symmetric T1 template, Serial Longitudinal Registration toolbox, bias correction, segmentation, registration to MNI, modulation with Jacobian determinants, 8mm FWHM smoothing. Statistical analyses: LMEM for longitudinal changes, voxelwise search with random field theory correction, nested LOOCV for machine learning predictions. This study uniquely examines GM morphological neuroplasticity (previous studies focused on functional activation or WM integrity) and importantly separates left and right hemispherotomy groups based on documented hemispheric specialization and differential post-damage plasticity patterns.


